 INSERT INTO items VALUES('BOB-240','Task','Completed (→ Fixed.md)','medium','workable-items close/update do not validate the status word against the item''s Type (§11.4.33) — extend CLI + validate invariant (BOB-239 mechanical-fix half)',unistr('WHAT: split from BOB-239 (closed 2026-09-25 after bulk-correcting 30\u000apre-existing §11.4.33 closure-vocabulary violations). This item is the\u000aremaining MECHANICAL-PREVENTION half: extend\u000aconstitution/scripts/workable-items'' `close` and `update` subcommands to\u000aVALIDATE the chosen status word against the item''s own Type (Bug->Fixed,\u000aFeature->Implemented, Task->Completed, any type->Obsolete) and REFUSE a\u000amismatched call rather than silently accepting it. Also extend the\u000a`validate` subcommand''s existing invariant set to catch this class for\u000adefense-in-depth — confirmed this session that `validate: OK` ran\u000arepeatedly against a DB simultaneously holding 30+ live violations of\u000athis exact class, so the current invariant set does not check it.\u000a\u000aEVIDENCE THIS IS A REAL, RECURRING MISTAKE, NOT A HYPOTHETICAL: this\u000asession''s own conductor made the identical error 4 times in a row\u000a(BOB-077/100/179/226, all Type=Task closed with `--status fixed`) before\u000aan unrelated self-audit caught it — on a DB that ALREADY held 30\u000ahistorical instances of the same mistake from earlier sessions. A\u000aCLI-level guard would have refused every one of those 34 calls at the\u000amoment they were made, instead of requiring a human/agent to remember to\u000aaudit for it afterward.\u000a\u000aSCOPE: constitution/scripts/workable-items/ (Go source) — a UNIVERSAL,\u000aconstitution-submodule-owned tool, per §11.4.17. Landing a real fix here\u000aneeds the §11.4.26 fetch/merge/push-to-all-upstreams workflow, same as\u000aBOB-191''s gate fix this session, NOT boba''s own commit-push-all.sh.\u000a\u000aACCEPTANCE: (1) `workable-items close --status <word>` refuses when\u000a<word>''s implied Type-mapping does not match the target item''s actual\u000aType, printing the correct word to use; (2) same for `update --status`;\u000a(3) `validate` gains a new invariant scanning every Fixed-location item\u000afor a Type/Status mismatch per the closed §11.4.33 mapping, FAILing (not\u000asilently passing) on any hit; (4) each of (1)-(3) ships a paired §1.1\u000amutation proving the check is load-bearing (a neutered version of the\u000acheck must let a known-bad Type/Status pair through); (5) the Obsolete\u000astatus is correctly treated as valid for ANY Type (it is not part of the\u000atype-specific mapping) so the new check does not false-positive on\u000alegitimately Obsolete-closed items.\u000a\u000aDISCOVERY CHANNEL (§11.4.238): found by the conductor''s own repeated,\u000aself-caught instances of the mistake this session, generalised into\u000aBOB-239 (the bulk-correction), now split into this item (the mechanical\u000aprevention) per BOB-239''s own acceptance criterion 2/3.'),NULL,NULL,NULL,'AI','AI','Fixed',unistr('## BOB-240 — workable-items close/update do not validate the status word against the item''s Type (§11.4.33) — extend CLI + validate invariant (BOB-239 mechanical-fix half)\u000a\u000a**Status:** Completed (→ Fixed.md)\u000a**Type:** Task\u000a**Evidence:** docs/qa/BOB-240/closure_evidence_20260925.md\u000a**Severity:** medium\u000a**Created-By:** AI\u000a**Assigned-To:** AI\u000a\u000aWHAT: split from BOB-239 (closed 2026-09-25 after bulk-correcting 30\u000apre-existing §11.4.33 closure-vocabulary violations). This item is the\u000aremaining MECHANICAL-PREVENTION half: extend\u000aconstitution/scripts/workable-items'' `close` and `update` subcommands to\u000aVALIDATE the chosen status word against the item''s own Type (Bug->Fixed,\u000aFeature->Implemented, Task->Completed, any type->Obsolete) and REFUSE a\u000amismatched call rather than silently accepting it. Also extend the\u000a`validate` subcommand''s existing invariant set to catch this class for\u000adefense-in-depth — confirmed this session that `validate: OK` ran\u000arepeatedly against a DB simultaneously holding 30+ live violations of\u000athis exact class, so the current invariant set does not check it.\u000a\u000aEVIDENCE THIS IS A REAL, RECURRING MISTAKE, NOT A HYPOTHETICAL: this\u000asession''s own conductor made the identical error 4 times in a row\u000a(BOB-077/100/179/226, all Type=Task closed with `--status fixed`) before\u000aan unrelated self-audit caught it — on a DB that ALREADY held 30\u000ahistorical instances of the same mistake from earlier sessions. A\u000aCLI-level guard would have refused every one of those 34 calls at the\u000amoment they were made, instead of requiring a human/agent to remember to\u000aaudit for it afterward.\u000a\u000aSCOPE: constitution/scripts/workable-items/ (Go source) — a UNIVERSAL,\u000aconstitution-submodule-owned tool, per §11.4.17. Landing a real fix here\u000aneeds the §11.4.26 fetch/merge/push-to-all-upstreams workflow, same as\u000aBOB-191''s gate fix this session, NOT boba''s own commit-push-all.sh.\u000a\u000aACCEPTANCE: (1) `workable-items close --status <word>` refuses when\u000a<word>''s implied Type-mapping does not match the target item''s actual\u000aType, printing the correct word to use; (2) same for `update --status`;\u000a(3) `validate` gains a new invariant scanning every Fixed-location item\u000afor a Type/Status mismatch per the closed §11.4.33 mapping, FAILing (not\u000asilently passing) on any hit; (4) each of (1)-(3) ships a paired §1.1\u000amutation proving the check is load-bearing (a neutered version of the\u000acheck must let a known-bad Type/Status pair through); (5) the Obsolete\u000astatus is correctly treated as valid for ANY Type (it is not part of the\u000atype-specific mapping) so the new check does not false-positive on\u000alegitimately Obsolete-closed items.\u000a\u000aDISCOVERY CHANNEL (§11.4.238): found by the conductor''s own repeated,\u000aself-caugh